  "question": {
    "text": "A series LCR circuit has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> and it is connected to ac voltage of amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. At frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math> lower than resonant frequency, the amplitude of current will be approximately"
  },
