  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>For an LCR circuit. the resonant&nbsp;angular frequency is given by, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>L</mi><mi>C</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>The given frequency is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;lower than resonant frequency. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Reactance of the capacitor at given frequency,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.</p><p>Reactance of the inductor at given frequency,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Now the amplitude of the&nbsp;current in the given circuit will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msqrt><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msubsup><mo>-</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>50</mn><msqrt><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>250</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>238</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
